 "start_model_cif_sha256": "fdd038f9fb877e7d12ac99fa9c0dc01d2bd72a9d15459e7f2f3d5884f3ae475c",
 "verdict": "Both 40 ns replicas end on a near-flat 5 ns block (+0.056, -0.109 A/ns), but that does NOT establish convergence: across the eight blocks of each run the block MEANS wander by 3.00 A and 2.80 A with the block slope changing sign 6 times and 3 times. The wander is larger than any trend, so a flat final block is luck of the window, and RMSD plateau is not a usable convergence criterion for this system at this length. What IS stable is the per-residue flexibility RANKING, which agrees across all four replicas, and that is all these runs support."
}